      "answer": "Martin Lopez joined Opeth in 1997, partway through the recording of \"My Arms, Your Hearse\" (1998). He replaced original drummer Anders Nordin, who had left the band, and went on to record five consecutive studio albums with Opeth: My Arms, Your Hearse (1998), [Still Life (1999)](/articles/still-life-drum-setup), [Blackwater Park (2001)](/articles/blackwater-park-drum-setup), [Deliverance (2002)](/articles/deliverance-drum-setup), and Damnation (2003), plus Ghost Reveries (2005), before leaving the band in 2006. My Arms, Your Hearse is the document of his first year in Opeth and the foundation of what would become one of progressive death metal's most influential drumming careers."
